    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268-a19">

                <pb facs="0704" n="614" sameAs="frus:frus1875v01/pg614"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 10 in No. 731.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Schenck to
                        Lord Derby.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-03-12"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 12,
                        1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: Referring to our correspondence in
                    relation to the American vessel “G. C. Trufant,” I beg leave to state to your
                    lordship that I have this moment received a telegram sent by the United States
                    consul at Liverpool to-day to the consul-general of the United States at London
                    in these words: “I have positive information that the “G. C. Trufant” has been
                    granted a British register previous to the 10th of this month. She will probably
                    sail to-morrow.”</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item>ROBT. C. SCHENCK.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Earl of Derby.</hi></item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
